    "result_text": "All tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a `namesakeCount` field \u2014 the number of existing owners (before this create) sharing the same firstName and lastName, case-insensitively \u2014 returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Approach (structural impact kept low):** rather than growing any existing method or class, the counting logic lives in one new small, self-contained function class with a single method and no surrounding complexity \u2014 mirroring the existing `AssignCustomerCode` step.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`CountNamesakes.java`** (new) \u2014 a small OfficeFloor function that counts existing namesakes via the repository and sets the value on the owner before save. No shared state, WMC_other = 0.\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `namesakes` step in the create pipeline (after `customerCode`, before `save`), so the count is taken before the new owner is persisted.\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `namesake_count` column field with a plain getter/setter (persisted so GET reflects the create-time snapshot per spec).\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema; MapStruct maps it by name automatically (no mapper edit needed).\n5. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** + **`data.sql`** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column and a trailing `NULL` to the ten positional seed inserts (the test profile is HSQLDB with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must be declared explicitly).\n\nFull test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `coreCountsNamesakes` acceptance test asserting `$.namesakeCount == 1`.",
